    "updated_at": "2022-07-05T15:24:01Z",
    "body": "Hi, sorry for the delayed answer.\r\n\r\nMaybe you're right and even a white space should be treated as default slot, but what about formatting your html, as web components can't be self closed, a format tool or even yourself can put something like\r\n```html\r\n<my-component\r\n  long-attr1=\"...long string\"\r\n  long-attr2=\"...long string\"\r\n  long-attr3=\"...long string\"\r\n  long-attr4=\"...long string\"\r\n>\r\n  <span slot=\"other\">\r\n    <!--more html-->\r\n  </span>\r\n</my-component>\r\n```\r\nMy team thought there is no fallback for default slot because of this, and IMHO I think it could make more troubles than solutions. How many web component could it be created with the intention of replacing a new line or a space for the default slot?\r\n\r\nIf a white space or a new line are relevant you can always use a escape char sequence isn't it?\r\n\r\nPlease tell me if I'm wrong but I think this could be problematic.\r\n\r\nRegarsd.\r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
